{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"p\">\n  <state id=\"p\" initial=\"a\">\n    <state id=\"a\">\n      <transition event=\"go\" target=\"b c\"/>\n    </state>\n    <state id=\"b\">\n      <transition event=\"go\" target=\"c\"/>\n    </state>\n    <final id=\"c\"/>\n  </state>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-conflicting-targets.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-conflicting-targets.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":2,"byteOffset":160,"endColumn":41,"endLine":4,"startColumn":39,"startLine":4},"insertedContent":{"text":""}}]}],"description":{"text":"remove the target `c`, keeping `b`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-conflicting-targets.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":41,"endLine":4,"startColumn":40,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"transition targets `b` and `c` cannot be active at the same time\n\n**Note:** both targets lie in different children of `p`, which is not a <parallel> and can have only one active child; a multi-target set must form a legal state configuration\n\n**Note:** removing `b` (keeping `c`) would leave `b` unreachable: no other transition, `initial`, or history default enters it\n\n**Help:** keep only one of these targets, or place them in different regions of a common `<parallel>` ancestor\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.11 Legal State Configurations and Specifications\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.5 <transition>","text":"transition targets `b` and `c` cannot be active at the same time"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":162,"start":161},"category":"semantic"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"only one child of this state can be active"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-conflicting-targets.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":9,"endLine":2,"startColumn":4,"startLine":2}}},{"id":2,"message":{"text":"`b` is entered here"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-conflicting-targets.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":39,"endLine":4,"startColumn":38,"startLine":4}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML030"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"the targets of a transition or an `initial` attribute must form a legal state configuration, and the compiler requires each pair to lie in different regions of a common `<parallel>`: targets in different children of a compound `<state>` would require two active children; a target and its own ancestor or descendant name one region twice (a state listed twice is only the `SCXML072` warning)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: keep only one of the conflicting targets and, when nothing else enters the other state, give it its own transition so it does not become unreachable (`SCXML029`); or move the targets into separate regions of a `<parallel>`. The suggested removal is offered only when it strands no state.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.11 Legal State Configurations and Specifications\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML030` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#LegalStateConfigurations","id":"SCXML030","name":"SCXML030","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a multi-target set cannot be active at the same time"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}